.TH FREXP 3
.SH NAME
frexp, ldexp, modf \- split into mantissa and exponent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
double
frexp(value, eptr)
double value;
int *eptr;

double
ldexp(value, exp)
double value;
int exp;

double
modf(value, iptr)
double value, *iptr;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B frexp
returns the mantissa of
.IR value :
a number
.I x
whose magnitude is at least 0.5 and less than 1, with the sign of
.IR value ;
and stores in *\fIeptr\fP the integer
.I n
such that
.I value
=
.I x
* 2^\fIn\fP. A zero value gives 0 for both.
.PP
.B ldexp
returns
.I value
* 2^\fIexp\fP.
.PP
.B modf
returns the fractional part of
.I value
and stores its integer part, toward zero, in *\fIiptr\fP; both have the
sign of
.IR value .
.PP
These are exact. They are in the C library, and need no
.BR \-lm .
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
When the result of ldexp is too large, it returns HUGE_VAL, an
infinity, with the sign of
.IR value ;
when it is too small, 0.
.SH ERRORS
ldexp sets errno to ERANGE when the result is too large or too small.
.SH SEE ALSO
floor(3), exp(3), intro(3)
.SH HISTORY
The
.BR frexp ,
.B ldexp
and
.B modf
functions are in Version 7 AT&T UNIX.
